~ start
The supermarket is way louder today than it usually is on a weekday. There are lots of long lines at the cashiers.

OLLIE: Wow... Nanay, why are there so many people here today? Everyone looks like they're in a super big hurry.

PILI: People are worried about the heavy rains coming. They're stocking up on groceries.

VALERIE: I don't get why everyone is panicking, Nay. Our baranggay never gets flooded anyway. 

PILI: Because it's always better to be safe, Valerie. Even if the storm doesn't hit us directly, the strong winds can still rip off a roof tile or crack a window in our house.

PILI: But today is about you, Ollie, okay? Since turning eight is a very special milestone, your Tatay and I decided to give you your very own budget!
PILI: Here is ₱125.00. You can go down the aisles and choose whatever decorations and treats you want for your party tomorrow!

VALERIE: Wow, Ollie! You're the big boss today. Don't go wasting it all on the expensive stuff, okay? Make sure to buy all you want within your budget!

OLLIE: I can do it! I'll pick the best ones.



#[CUE TO MINIGAME]
Wallet Balance - ₱125.00
Complete the party list without running out of coins!


STATION 1: Birthday Balloons

PILI: Alright, Ollie. We have enough coins left over for a pack of balloons to hang near the dining table. Which ones do you want for tomorrow?

- Bright Yellow Pack (₱12.00)
	VALERIE: Good choice, Ollie. Yellow is bright. It'll make the living room look nice and cozy.
	Yellow is a happy color. I like it.

- Metallic Multi-Color Pack (₱18.00) 
	KIKI: Shiny! Look, Ate! Shiny!
	VALERIE: They cost six pesos more, Ollie! If they pop easily, I'm blaming you.


STATION 2: Party Hats

VALERIE: Look, Ollie. They have birthday hats here. Pick the design you like best, but don't take too long!

- Shiny Silver Hats (₱22.00)
	OLLIE: These look like space helmets. Kuya Dodong will pretend he's an alien if he wears this.
	KIKI: Shiny! Give baby!

- Colorful Polka-Dot Hats (₱15.00)
	VALERIE: These are classic. And look, they're seven pesos cheaper than the silver ones. Nanay can use that for the matchboxes.
	Polka dots are fun. They look like giant candy drops.


STATION 3: Birthday Banner

VALERIE: We need the birthday banner to hang up on the wall. Tatay can use some thumbtacks to stick it up. Which cartoon design do you want?

- Superhero Team Banner (₱25.00)
	VALERIE: Ooh, this one looks so cool! Dodong is definitely going to try and copy the superhero poses when we hang it up.
	Superheroes...I like it!

- The Animated Robot-Car Banner (₱20.00)
	OLLIE: This one has the giant transforming robot-cars on it. Ritchie has the exact same banner hanging in his house for his birthday parties.
	KIKI: Robot! Vroom-vroom! See robot!


STATION 4: Spaghetti Sauce

PILI: Your father already bought the pasta from the sari-sari store, so we just need the sauce. Which flavor should we get for your party, Ollie? 

- Sweet-Style Sauce (₱23.50)
	This is the best! It's super sweet, especially when Nanay mixes in the condensed milk and sliced red hotdogs.
	VALERIE: Classic sweet style. Noni is going to eat three whole plates of this and get red sauce all over his ears.

- Hot and Spicy Sauce (₱26.00) 
	VALERIE: Spicy?! Ollie, you know Noni cries if his tongue burns even a little bit!
	OLLIE: I picked it because Kuya Dodong always brags that he can eat spicy food like a real adult. I want to see if he's lying.

STATION 5: Marshmallows for Hotdog Sticks

PILI: The red hotdogs are settled. Now we need the marshmallows to skewer on the tips of the bamboo sticks! Tatay already whittled the bamboo barbecue sticks for us back home. Let's pick the marshmallow toppings.

- Mega-Sized White Marshmallows (₱14.00)
	VALERIE: Woah! They're a lot bigger than the normal ones.
	These are Kuya Dodong's favorite. He always tries to stuff three of them in his mouth at the same time to look like a chubby bunny.

- Pastel Rainbow Marshmallows (₱18.00)
	KIKI: Pink! Green! Pretty!
	VALERIE: They cost five pesos more but they’ll make the serving platter look like a real fiesta. Noni is going to lose his mind when he sees the colors.


STATION 6: Cake Frosting

PILI: And now for the best part. The frosting for your chocolate cake! I already found the cocoa powder so we just need the topping mix. Which style should we get?

- Rich Fudge Chocolate Frosting (₱28.00)
	Ritchie loves chocolate fudge. He always gets it all over his chin at parties.
	VALERIE: Double chocolate! That’s going to make the cake look incredibly thick and delicious, Nay.

- Sweet Milk Chocolate Frosting (₱25.00)
	PILI: Milk chocolate is a great choice, Ollie. It's a bit lighter and sweeter and it reminds me of the warm cocoa we drink on rainy mornings.
	KIKI: Yum-yum! 


RESULT 1 - High Spender (Remaining Balance - ₱0.00 - ₱3.00)

VALERIE: Susmariosep, Ollie, look at that. We barely have enough coins left for the tricycle ride back to Taklub!

KIKI: Ate... loud... No fighting... 

PILI: It’s alright, Valerie. We made it work. Look how happy your brother is. We still have everything we need to make tomorrow special.

VALERIE: I know, Nay. It's just... if it starts pouring right now, the tricycle drivers are going to charge us double fare. Plus they always don't have spare change.

VALERIE: Just... help me unload the basket onto the counter later, Ollie. 
 


RESULT 2 - Balanced Spender (Remaining Balance - ₱4.00 - ₱10.00)

VALERIE: Okay, not bad. We got it all and we still have a tiny bit of change left over. You did a good job balancing your budget, Ollie.

KIKI: Cake! Big cake for uya!



RESULT 3 - Practical Budgeter (Remaining Balance - ₱11.00+)

VALERIE: Wow. Look at that, Nay! Ollie picked all the classic choices and saved us over fifteen pesos. We have more than enough left over to buy the extra matchboxes and the emergency candles!

PILI: Thank you, anak. You really know how to look after our blessings. Your Tatay will be very proud of you when we get home.


=> END